    <estimated-effort>10-16 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Implement Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Worker/Dispatch/ProvisioningHandlerDispatcher.cs per DS-2 §2.2-2.7 exactly: a BackgroundService hosting a ServiceBusSessionProcessor (CreateSessionProcessor, NOT CreateProcessor) against the sprk-provisioning-jobs queue, with MaxConcurrentSessions=DispatcherOptions.MaxConcurrentCustomers (default 4), MaxConcurrentCallsPerSession=1 (HARD-CODED, not a config value), MaxAutoLockRenewalDuration=DispatcherOptions.MaxHandlerDuration (default 01:05:00), PrefetchCount=0. Implement the 8-step message-handling flow from DS-2 §2.5 verbatim: deserialize envelope -&gt; resolve keyed handler -&gt; Level-2 idempotency gate -&gt; load run (OrphanRun / terminal-status short-circuit) -&gt; invoke handler (never trust it not to throw) -&gt; re-read run + apply outcome via IHandlerOutcomeApplier -&gt; mark processed + release lock -&gt; complete message for both Success and applied-Failure (Abandon reserved for infra faults at steps 3/6 only).</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Azure.Messaging.ServiceBus session processors, .NET keyed DI, BackgroundService lifecycle, and the BFF's ServiceBusJobProcessor pattern this class mirrors-and-diverges-from.</role>

  <goal>ProvisioningHandlerDispatcher.cs exists as a BackgroundService in .Worker, registered via AddHostedService, using CreateSessionProcessor with MaxConcurrentCallsPerSession hard-coded to 1 (protected by a forcing-function unit test per DS-2b R3), implementing the full 8-step dispatch flow with the exact dead-letter-reason table from DS-2 §2.8 (InvalidFormat / NoHandler / HandlerResolutionFailed / OrphanRun / OutcomeApplyFailed). DispatchCoreAsync is a pure, unit-testable decision function (no ServiceBusReceivedMessage dependency) per DS-2 §2.2. Shutdown mirrors the BFF's defensive StopProcessingAsync + DisposeAsync pattern including ObjectDisposedException tolerance.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>DS-2 (owner-locked design) specifies the L2 dispatcher as a mirror-and-diverge of the BFF's ServiceBusJobProcessor.cs (265 lines, read in full by DS-2 §1): same BackgroundService+processor+events shape, but session-aware (not the BFF's plain processor), keyed-DI handler resolution (not enumerate-and-match -- constructing 20 handler dependency graphs per message is wasteful and a single broken graph would poison every handler's dispatch), 65-min lock renewal (handlers run 10-60 min per DS-2b §1.2), and retry authority in §4C RollbackTransitions rather than an SB Abandon-loop (L2 has an explicit rollback taxonomy the BFF does not). DS-2b's adversarial re-examination of 5 alternatives (ETag-retry, conditional-patch, TransactionalBatch, Redis lock, event-sourcing) confirmed session-serialization is the best-practice answer: it costs ~1h on a ~27h E2E process (dominated by the 24h SPE gate) and eliminates, by transport-level construction, the systematic ETag-conflict class every alternative would otherwise have to survive.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Worker/Dispatch/ProvisioningHandlerDispatcher.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Dispatch/DispatcherOptions.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Dispatch/DispatchDecision.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Dispatch/DispatchModule.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Worker/Program.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/ServiceBusJobProcessor.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Enqueue/ServiceBusHandlerEnqueuer.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Reconciler/StateReconcilerService.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="100" status="pending">.Worker project must exist to host the dispatcher</dependency>
      <dependency task="101" status="pending">.Worker App Service resource must exist as the deploy target for eventual live testing</dependency>
      <dependency task="103" status="pending">HandlerIds catalog + keyed registrations must exist for GetKeyedService&lt;IProvisioningHandler&gt; resolution to succeed -- author 102 and 103 together or sequence 103 first if a strict build order is preferred</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec.md FR-22">L2 handler execution is session-serialized per customer: ServiceBusSessionProcessor with SessionId=CustomerId, MaxConcurrentCallsPerSession=1 is a HARD-CODED correctness invariant (not a tunable) protecting the 39 ETag-guarded ReplaceRunAsync call sites from cross-handler races (DS-2b Sec.0-1). Retry authority is Sec.4C RollbackTransitions, never an SB Abandon-loop.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design.md §4.2b">The dispatcher owns dequeue + handler invocation + outcome-apply wiring; it MUST NOT compute DAG ready-sets itself. StateReconcilerService/DagAdvancer remain the single source of truth for ready-set computation (DS-2 Sec.5) -- the dispatcher calls IHandlerOutcomeApplier.ApplyHandlerOutcomeAsync and nothing else.</constraint>
    <constraint source="DS-2 §2.6">App Service graceful shutdown (~30s, extendable via WEBSITES_CONTAINER_STOP_TIME_LIMIT) can NEVER drain a 30-60 min handler -- the dispatcher MUST NOT pretend otherwise. An interrupted handler's message lock expires, SB redelivers, Level-2 lock has also expired, re-invoke happens, L3 CompletedPhases dedup no-ops the completed portion. Recommend WEBSITES_CONTAINER_STOP_TIME_LIMIT=00:05:00 (documented for the Bicep task, not set here).</constraint>
    <constraint source="DS-2 §2.8">Handler DOMAIN failures never dead-letter -- they land as §4C Cosmos transitions via IHandlerOutcomeApplier with full operator visibility. Only 5 reasons dead-letter: InvalidFormat, NoHandler, HandlerResolutionFailed, OrphanRun, OutcomeApplyFailed (MaxDeliveryCount exceeded).</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11">Three-question component-justification gate applies to any NEW class/interface/Bicep resource/script this task introduces. Existing/Extension/Cost-of-doing-nothing are pre-answered in &lt;notes&gt; below; cite them verbatim in the PR description per root CLAUDE.md §11 enforcement table.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>ProvisioningHandlerDispatcher BackgroundService</topic>
    <files>
