    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Session processor mirror-and-diverge" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/ServiceBusJobProcessor.cs">Same BackgroundService+processor+events shape; diverges on CreateSessionProcessor, keyed-DI resolution, 65min lock renewal, and §4C retry authority instead of SB Abandon-loop (DS-2 §1.5 table).</pattern>
      <pattern name="3-level idempotency" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/IdempotencyService.cs">L1 SB MessageId dedup (enqueuer-side, exists) + L2 Redis lock (this task's DispatchIdempotencyService, task 105) + L3 CompletedPhases scan (exists per handler).</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL). Read ServiceBusJobProcessor.cs in full, then DS-2 §2 in full.</step>
    <step order="1" name="DispatcherOptions">Author DispatcherOptions.cs: Enabled(true), MaxConcurrentCustomers(4), MaxHandlerDuration(01:05:00), SessionIdleTimeout(00:00:30), MaxDeliveryCount(5) -- bound from config section 'Dispatcher'.</step>
    <step order="2" name="DispatchDecision">Author the DispatchDecision record: Complete | DeadLetter(reason, description) | Abandon.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Dispatcher class">Author ProvisioningHandlerDispatcher : BackgroundService per DS-2 §2.2 constructor shape (ServiceBusClient, IServiceScopeFactory, IOptions&lt;DispatcherOptions&gt;, IOptions&lt;ServiceBusModuleOptions&gt;, TimeProvider, ILogger). ExecuteAsync creates the session processor with the exact options block from DS-2 §2.2, wires OnSessionMessageAsync + OnErrorAsync, StartProcessingAsync, then parks.</step>
    <step order="4" name="DispatchCoreAsync">Implement the pure decision function per DS-2 §2.5's 8-step flow, operating on (HandlerEnvelope envelope, int deliveryCount, IServiceProvider scopedProvider, CancellationToken) -&gt; Task&lt;DispatchDecision&gt;, with NO ServiceBusReceivedMessage dependency (event wrapper translates the decision into Complete/DeadLetter/Abandon calls).</step>
    <step order="5" name="Wire outcome applier">Consume IHandlerOutcomeApplier (task 104's extraction) from the per-message scope for step 6 of the flow; do not re-implement §4C logic in the dispatcher.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Shutdown">Override StopAsync mirroring ServiceBusJobProcessor.cs's defensive finally block (StopProcessingAsync + DisposeAsync with ObjectDisposedException tolerance).</step>
    <step order="7" name="Register">AddHostedService&lt;ProvisioningHandlerDispatcher&gt; in .Worker Program.cs via a DispatchModule.AddDispatchModule(services, config) extension per ADR-010.</step>
    <step order="8" name="Forcing-function test">Author a unit test asserting the constructed ServiceBusSessionProcessorOptions.MaxConcurrentCallsPerSession == 1 -- DS-2b R3: protect this invariant from config drift, it is correctness not tuning.</step>
    <step order="9" name="Build + verify">dotnet build 0 errors; dotnet format; zero analyzer warnings.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If DispatchCoreAsync's Cosmos re-read at step 6 (post-handler-invoke, fresh ETag) shows the outcome applier returning Conflict repeatedly under a single-writer session (which should be structurally impossible per DS-2b's whole thesis), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 -- this would indicate a non-handler writer (endpoint, QuarantineClearService, reconciler) is racing the dispatcher outside the documented R1 rider (DS-2b §9), which is a design violation, not a code bug to patch around.</trigger>
  </escalation>

