  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">ProvisioningHandlerDispatcher is registered via AddHostedService in .Worker Program.cs; hosted service starts on app start, stops cleanly on shutdown (integration smoke).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Unit test asserts the constructed ServiceBusSessionProcessorOptions has MaxConcurrentCallsPerSession == 1 -- test FAILS if a future edit changes this to a config-bound value (DS-2b R3 forcing function).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">DispatchCoreAsync given bad-JSON input returns DeadLetter(InvalidFormat); given unknown HandlerId returns DeadLetter(NoHandler); given a processed-marker hit returns Complete-without-invoke; given lock-held returns Abandon; given OrphanRun (run doc absent) returns DeadLetter(OrphanRun); given a terminal-status run (Cancelled/Quarantined/Completed) returns Complete-without-invoke.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">grep 'CreateSessionProcessor' in ProvisioningHandlerDispatcher.cs returns exactly 1 match; grep 'CreateProcessor(' (non-session) returns 0 matches.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Worker/ exits 0; dotnet test (Dispatch/* tests) exits 0.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11): Existing -- BFF's ServiceBusJobProcessor is BFF-scoped (ADR-010 forbids L2 handlers registering in BFF) and is NOT session-aware, so it cannot be reused as-is. Extension -- cannot extend a non-session processor into a session processor without rewriting its core loop; DS-2 §1.5 documents every divergence point explicitly. Cost-of-doing-nothing -- without this class, zero handlers ever execute end-to-end; this is THE load-bearing gap FR-18/SC#5 identifies. Owner sign-off item (DS-2 §7.1, reaffirmed DS-2b §9): session-serialized execution is adopted as designed.</notes>

